rounds.parentBrief:
Forming a tight living circle in the center of the wide, windswept Lindenhof plaza, the four boys huddle against the cold night. In the very center facing the camera, Levin — a preschooler with wavy light blonde hair, wearing a green fleece jacket, dark blue trousers, and brown boots — sits cross-legged, holding the dull greyish-red dragon egg pressed firmly against his chest inside his widely opened jacket, his arms wrapped tight around it. Max, seen from behind on the left, wears his orange pullover, dark brown corduroy dungarees, grey wool socks, and black rubber boots; he sits with his back to the viewer, head tucked toward the egg, brow tense and mouth shut. Kiaan, seen from behind on the right, wears his deep purple hooded sweatshirt, olive trousers, and white trainers; he presses his back into the huddle, head tucked down. Julian, seen from behind behind Levin, wears his yellow anorak, grey trousers, and dark blue boots; his back forms a solid block behind his brother, his head tilted toward the egg. Planted firmly in the left foreground, the large Bernese Mountain Dog Nia sits upright, completing the living shelter. Levin's red wool cap remains hidden inside the dark hole in the Lindenhofbrunnen wall. The wide shot emphasizes their intense shared effort against the dark, cold autumn night.

